WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.331 --> 00:00:16.732
weird to think that someone from our neighborhood is a thief," Cole said.

2
00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:19.693
"I know," Henry agreed.

3
00:00:19.713 --> 00:00:24.994
"But Maggie's money is gone, which means that someone stole it.

4
00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.795
All we have to do now is figure out who it was."

5
00:00:28.815 --> 00:00:30.656
"Who are the suspects again?"

6
00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:31.836
Cole asked.

7
00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:33.704
Maggie sighed.

8
00:00:33.724 --> 00:00:35.625
"Weren't you listening?"

9
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:36.666
she said.

10
00:00:36.686 --> 00:00:42.308
"There were only a few people close enough to the lemonade stand to grab the money.

11
00:00:43.188 --> 00:00:45.609
They were Nathan and Nora, Mrs.

12
00:00:45.689 --> 00:00:49.871
Martin and Marty, Ryan, and those two teenage girls."

13
00:00:49.891 --> 00:00:52.652
"I doubt it was Nathan," Cole said.

14
00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:54.293
"He's a nice kid."

15
00:00:55.213 --> 00:00:55.994
Henry nodded.

16
00:00:57.294 --> 00:01:00.736
Nathan was the same age as him and Cole, and everyone liked him.

17
00:01:01.668 --> 00:01:05.329
Kids liked him because he was always smiling and loved to have fun.

18
00:01:05.509 --> 00:01:10.390
"That little sister of his is kind of weird though," Maggie pointed out.

19
00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:16.232
"She's always making up crazy stories and dressing up in funny costumes and stuff."

20
00:01:17.392 --> 00:01:20.653
"Nora is a bit strange," Henry agreed.

21
00:01:20.673 --> 00:01:24.454
"But being weird isn't the same as being a thief.

22
00:01:25.414 --> 00:01:27.575
Plus she's only five years old.

23
00:01:28.315 --> 00:01:32.744
That's pretty young to steal money from a cashbox."

24
00:01:32.764 --> 00:01:35.987
"What about Ryan, that kid who skateboards all the time?"

25
00:01:36.387 --> 00:01:37.028
Maggie said.

26
00:01:37.048 --> 00:01:40.170
"He's always getting in trouble at school."

27
00:01:41.271 --> 00:01:43.652
Ryan was three years younger than Henry.

28
00:01:44.493 --> 00:01:47.595
Henry had seen him around, but he didn't know Ryan very well.

29
00:01:47.615 --> 00:01:50.217
"What kind of trouble?"

30
00:01:50.698 --> 00:01:51.819
Henry asked Maggie.

31
00:01:52.739 --> 00:01:53.360
She shrugged.

32
00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:58.724
"Mostly teachers get mad at him for goofing off and not paying attention in class."

33
00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:03.059
"I heard he skateboarded into his neighbor's flowers," Cole said.

34
00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:05.481
"He got in big trouble for that!"

35
00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:09.544
"That doesn't make him a thief," Henry said.

36
00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:13.748
"But he seems like a better suspect than the others.

37
00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:16.009
Let's go find him and talk to him."

38
00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.853
Maggie put a cover on her pitcher of lemonade so bugs wouldn't get in it.

39
00:02:21.394 --> 00:02:25.317
Then the three kids headed down the block in the direction that Ryan had gone.

40
00:02:26.198 --> 00:02:27.639
"What are we going to say when we find him?"

41
00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:28.680
Cole asked.

42
00:02:29.668 --> 00:02:31.249
"I know what I want to say."

43
00:02:31.609 --> 00:02:32.389
Maggie frowned.

44
00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:35.351
"I want to tell him to give me back my money!

45
00:02:36.211 --> 00:02:38.412
Otherwise I'll break his skateboard in half!"

46
00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:42.674
"I don't think that's a good idea, Maggie," Henry told her.

47
00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:45.215
"We're not going to threaten Ryan.

48
00:02:46.135 --> 00:02:51.358
We're just going to ask him a few questions, like my dad does when he's interviewing someone."

49
00:02:52.118 --> 00:02:56.000
Henry's father was a journalist who wrote stories for the local newspaper.

50
00:02:56.928 --> 00:03:02.410
He liked to say that his job was one part writing, one part asking questions, and three parts

51
00:03:02.511 --> 00:03:08.653
listening. That was because he spent so much time interviewing people and listening to their answers.

52
00:03:08.673 --> 00:03:12.335
"Wait. We're going to ask Ryan a few questions?"

53
00:03:12.835 --> 00:03:13.435
Cole said.

54
00:03:13.455 --> 00:03:16.897
"I can only think of one question: Did you take the money?"

55
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:19.158
"Yeah," Maggie said.

56
00:03:19.178 --> 00:03:21.059
"And I already asked him that."

57
00:03:21.899 --> 00:03:23.900
Henry had just spotted Ryan up ahead.

58
00:03:24.684 --> 00:03:26.805
The skateboarder was practicing kick flips.

59
00:03:27.725 --> 00:03:32.207
His baggy shorts fluttered when he jumped, and his sneakers squeaked when he landed.

60
00:03:32.227 --> 00:03:37.309
"Just listen and play along," Henry whispered to Cole and Maggie.

61
00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:40.971
"I'm going to interview Ryan, just like Dad would.

62
00:03:41.891 --> 00:03:44.512
We might learn something by listening to his answers."

63
00:03:45.492 --> 00:03:47.113
The other two looked skeptical.

64
00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.454
But Henry hurried forward.

65
00:03:49.474 --> 00:03:51.935
"Hi, Ryan," he called out.

66
00:03:51.955 --> 00:03:54.456
"Can I talk to you for a second?"

67
00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:59.030
Ryan finished his flip, and then rolled over to Henry on his skateboard.

68
00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.771
"Sure, dude.

69
00:04:01.752 --> 00:04:03.113
What do you want to talk about?"

70
00:04:04.093 --> 00:04:06.655
He grinned, shoving both hands in his pockets.

71
00:04:07.575 --> 00:04:08.616
Henry smiled back.

72
00:04:08.636 --> 00:04:12.898
"We're just trying to find out what happened to Maggie's money.

73
00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:16.460
Since you were there, we thought you might have seen who took it."

74
00:04:17.321 --> 00:04:18.722
"Nope. Sorry."

75
00:04:19.122 --> 00:04:19.902
Ryan shrugged.

76
00:04:19.922 --> 00:04:22.484
"Okay," Henry said.

77
00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:26.717
"Then did you see anyone hanging around the lemonade stand?

78
00:04:27.417 --> 00:04:28.898
Maybe a stranger or something?"

79
00:04:28.918 --> 00:04:34.419
"I already told you there was nobody else around, Henry," Maggie interrupted.

80
00:04:35.279 --> 00:04:36.660
Then she glared at Ryan.

81
00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:39.480
"I know you stole my money.

82
00:04:40.681 --> 00:04:41.981
Why don't you just admit it?"

83
00:04:42.001 --> 00:04:43.742
"No way."

84
00:04:44.162 --> 00:04:45.382
Ryan glared back at her.

85
00:04:46.042 --> 00:04:48.663
"Why should I admit to something I didn't do?

86
00:04:49.203 --> 00:04:50.523
I didn't take your money!"

87
00:04:50.543 --> 00:04:53.572
"Well, somebody did," Cole pointed out.

88
00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:56.093
"It was probably her."

89
00:04:56.573 --> 00:04:58.554
Ryan laughed and pointed at Maggie.

90
00:04:58.574 --> 00:05:01.454
"What?" Maggie screeched.

91
00:05:01.474 --> 00:05:03.035
"Don't be ridiculous!

92
00:05:03.315 --> 00:05:05.195
Why would I steal my own money?"

93
00:05:05.916 --> 00:05:06.976
Ryan shrugged again.

94
00:05:06.996 --> 00:05:08.476
"How should I know?"

95
00:05:09.297 --> 00:05:11.117
Henry looked away, thinking.

96
00:05:12.537 --> 00:05:18.459
He still believed that Ryan was the most likely suspect, but this interview wasn't going well so far.

97
00:05:19.699 --> 00:05:21.560
Henry tried to think of another question.

98
00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.321
What would his dad ask?

99
00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:25.263
He couldn't think of anything.

100
00:05:26.163 --> 00:05:30.266
Besides he was pretty sure that Ryan wouldn't answer any more questions.

101
00:05:31.187 --> 00:05:33.989
Not after Maggie had just accused him of the crime again.

102
00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.051
So how could they figure out if Ryan had done it?
